	# --- /home: each person sees only their own things ------------------------
	# GATED, and that gate is what supplies the identity. Caddy runs
	# forward_auth first and copies the result in as X-Auth-Email; the landing
	# app reads that header and draws only the cards that account can open.
	# A browser cannot forge it -- whatever a client sends is replaced here.
	#
	# HIDING A CARD IS NOT WHAT PROTECTS IT. Every path those cards point at is
	# separately gated further down this file, and still refuses somebody who
	# types the URL. This page decides what is OFFERED, not what is allowed.
	# --- /find: one box for recipes, workouts, documents and code -------------
