	# --- /read/: Kavita, the EPUB and PDF reader ------------------------------
	# Jason, 2026-09-10: "I would like a PDF reader and an epub reader".
	#
	# NOT handle_path, and that distinction is the whole reason this works.
	# Kavita is an Angular SPA: strip the prefix and it serves an index.html
	# whose asset and API URLs are all rooted at /, which 404 against this
	# site. That is exactly how Stirling broke under /pdf/.
	#
	# So the prefix SURVIVES, and Kavita is told to expect it -- BaseUrl is
	# set to "/read/" in its appsettings.json. The app then builds its own
	# links correctly and there is nothing to rewrite.
	#
	# GATED, but Kavita also keeps its own login, and that is deliberate
	# rather than lazy. Kavita has its own user system with its own
	# per-library permissions; the household gate cannot express those. Two
	# doors is the honest arrangement until its OIDC (0.8.8+) is pointed at
	# /auth/oidc, which collapses them into one.
	handle /read/* {
		forward_auth https://192.168.1.86 {
			import nuc_gate
			uri /verify
			copy_headers X-Auth-Email
			header_up X-Forwarded-Uri {http.request.orig_uri}
		}
